.SP p2
.L 47.69 38.70
\f[NSR]\s[8]Cora grew up torn between her American father's
.L 57.69 38.70
\f[NSR]\s[8]stage magic and her Japanese mother's line of
.L 67.69 38.70
\f[NSR]\s[8]Shinto priestesses, always trusting the former over
.L 77.69 38.70
\f[NSR]\s[8]the latter — until she alone witnessed a malevolent
.L 87.69 38.70
\f[NSR]\s[8]spirit cause her father's death during a
.L 97.69 38.70
\f[NSR]\s[8]performance. Devastated and forced to reckon with
.L 107.69 38.70
\f[NSR]\s[8]truths she'd always dismissed, she returned to her
.L 117.69 38.70
\f[NSR]\s[8]mother to learn the family's real power, and now
.L 127.69 38.70
\f[NSR]\s[8]runs a paranormal detective agency, hoping one
.L 137.69 38.70
\f[NSR]\s[8]day to find the entity responsible.
.L 367.69 217.40
\f[NSR]\s[8]Guarded and sharp-tongued, Cora treats
.L 377.69 217.40
\f[NSR]\s[8]her true feelings the way she treats her
.L 387.69 217.40
\f[NSR]\s[8]tricks — always hidden behind whatever
.L 397.69 217.40
\f[NSR]\s[8]face she wants the world to see, making
.L 407.69 217.40
\f[NSR]\s[8]her almost impossible to really know.
.CP
.SH
\&Cora: Attacks
.PP
\&Spade: Cora fans out a hand of cards, which can deflect attacks and be thrown as a unit.
.PP
\&Diamond: Cora throws a card with dazzling precision slicing through anything like butter.
.PP
\&Heart: Cora places a card against the chest of a battered foe, which explodes into a series of spiritual, binding chains.
.PP
\&Club: Once placed, nothing can stop this blast.
.SH
\&Cora: Talismans
.PP
\&Cora's family power is traditionally channeled through paper talismans, but she prefers to work with something more familiar: playing cards. Beyond her attacks, these cards can also be empowered to hinder others.
